  "source_target_review": "Manual source-target review of the explicit business firmware with observation counters. services_main reaches one static firmware_owner through a138_ble_business_firmware_init/pump. Initialization constructs mailbox/data buses using a138_business_mmio_bus and a138_record_mmio_bus, whose four static direct-MMIO adapters are the only targets. a138_ble_business_init copies those fields once; no reachable code reassigns callbacks or installs another bus. Each mailbox-typed indirect caller conservatively includes business_mmio_read/write; each record-typed caller includes record_mmio_read/write. The complete-key request-facts inspection uses only the existing data bus. Two uint32 diagnostic counters increment only after successful CLAIM and COMPLETE and never enter task, ID, transfer or timeout decisions. The firmware observation step reads existing owner fields and writes two fixed f800 diagnostic addresses through inline volatile MMIO/fences. The fixed 16-page switch is compiled without jump tables and does not add an indirect target. No callback field, foreign bus, heap, PCM copy, recursive callback, interrupt or owner reentry is introduced. All selected source/header/linker/startup/provenance identities, complete actual RV32 disassembly and every reachable JALR site/target set are bound here; changed inputs, unknown callers or missing sites must fail. Direct-MMIO faults still use the existing CPU trap/halt policy; injected host callback-error recovery is not claimed as hard-core execution evidence.",
